<title>UK: NatWest launches $5.0 bln securitisation.</title>
<headline>NatWest launches $5.0 bln securitisation.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>NatWest Markets said it officially launched an 11-tranche asset-backed floating-rate issue worth approximately $5.0 billion in the name R.O.S.E. Funding.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p>    CLASS   RATING   AMT (MLN)   MARGIN   AVG LIFE</p>
<p>    A1(a)   Aa2/AA   750 USD	8	 0.88 YEARS</p>
<p>    A1(b)   Aa2/AA   600 STG	8	 0.75</p>
<p>    A2(a)   Aa2/AA   750 USD     18	 2.99</p>
<p>    A2(b)   Aa2/AA   600 STG     18	 3.02</p>
<p>    A3(a)   Aa2/AA   500 USD     22	 4.36</p>
<p>    A3(b)   Aa2/AA   600 STG     22	 4.28</p>
<p>    A4(a)   A	   25 USD     40	 5.00</p>
<p>    A4(b)   A	   16 STG     40	 5.00</p>
<p>    A5(a)   BBB	 27 USD     65	 5.00</p>
<p>    A5(b)   BBB	 18 STG     65	 5.00</p>
<p>    B	 =	  100 USD	=	 =</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p>All Class A tranches have an issue and reoffer price of par.</p>
<p>All Class A margins are over three-month LIBOR.</p>
<p>All Class A tranche legal maturities are in November 2001.</p>
<p>Average life assumes no substitution or prepayment.  </p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p>CLASS  PAYDATE  FEES (M/U, SELL)</p>
<p>    A1(a)  29.NOV   0.10 (0.05, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A1(b)  29.NOV   0.10 (0.05, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A2(a)  06.DEC   0.1875 (0.1375, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A2(b)  06.DEC   0.1875 (0.1375, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A3(a)  16.DEC   0.225 (0.1775, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A3(b)  16.DEC   0.225 (0.1775, 0.05)</p>
<p>    A4(a)  29.NOV   undisclosed</p>
<p>    A4(b)  29.NOV   undisclosed</p>
<p>    A5(a)  29.NOV   undisclosed</p>
<p>    A5(b)  29.NOV   undisclosed</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p>Interest payment months -- February, May, August, November</p>
<p>Denominations	     -- 100,000 (USD or GBP)</p>
<p>Negative pledge, IPMA 2 force majeure, no cross default</p>
<p>London listing. English law. 144A eligible</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p>R.O.S.E. Funding = Repeat Offering Securitisation Entity</p>
<p>Funding No.1 Ltd</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
</text>
